{
  "title": "11: Hud هود",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nالٓرٰ كِتٰبٌ اُحْكِمَتْ اٰيٰتُهٗ ثُمَّ فُصِّلَتْ مِنْ لَّدُنْ حَكِيْمٍ خَبِيْرٍۙ‏(1)\nALAARAA KETAABUM AUHKEMAT AAYAATOHU SUMMA FUSSELAT MIN LADUN HAKEEMIN KHABEERIN.\nA. L. R. (This is) a Book, with verses basic or fundamental (of established meaning), further explained in detail, from One Who is Wise and Well-acquainted (with all things): \nاَلَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَ ؕ اِنَّنِىْ لَكُمْ مِّنْهُ نَذِيْرٌ وَّبَشِيْرٌ ۙ‏(2)\nALLAA TA’BODOO ILLAA LAAHA INNANEE LAKUM MINHO NAZEERUM WWABASHEERUN.\n(It teacheth) that ye should worship none but Allah. (Say): “Verily I am (sent) unto you from Him to warn and to bring glad tidings: \nوَّاَنِ اسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يُمَتِّعْكُمْ مَّتَاعًا حَسَنًا اِلٰٓى اَجَلٍ مُّسَمًّى وَ يُؤْتِ كُلَّ ذِىْ فَضْلٍ فَضْلَهٗ ؕ وَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ كَبِيْرٍ‏(3)\nWA ASTAGHFEROOA TAQUL SUMMA TOOBOOA ELAYHE YUMATTEA’KUM MATAA-A’N HASANAN ELAA ELAA AJALIM WA YUTE KULLA ZEE FAZLIN FAZLAH WA TAWALLAW FA-INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN KABEER.\n“(And to preach thus), 'Seek ye the forgiveness of your Lord, and turn to Him in repentance; that He may grant you enjoyment, good (and true), for a term appointed, and bestow His abounding grace on all who abound in merit! But if ye turn away, then I fear for you the penalty of a great day: \nاِلَى اللّٰهِ مَرْجِعُكُمْۚ وَهُوَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(4)\nELAL LAAHE MARJE-O’KUM WA HOWA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\n'To Allah is your return, and He hath power over all things.'“ \nاَلَاۤ اِنَّهُمْ يَثْنُوْنَ صُدُوْرَهُمْ لِيَسْتَخْفُوْا مِنْهُؕ اَلَا حِيْنَ يَسْتَغْشُوْنَ ثِيَابَهُمْۙ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّوْنَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُوْنَۚ اِنَّهٗ عَلِيْمٌۢ بِذَاتِ الصُّدُوْرِ‏(5)\nALAA INNAHUM YASNOONA SUDOORAHUM LEESTAKHFOOA MENHU ALAA HEENA YASTAGHSHOONA SEEABAHUM YA’LAMO MAA YOSIRROONA WA MAA MAA YO’LENOON INNAHU A’LEEM BE-ZAATIS SODOOR.\nBehold! they fold up their hearts, that they may lie hid from Him! Ah even when they cover themselves with their garments, He knoweth what they conceal, and what they reveal: for He knoweth well the (inmost secrets) of the hearts. \nوَمَا مِنْ دَآ بَّةٍ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ رِزْقُهَا وَ يَعْلَمُ مُسْتَقَرَّهَا وَمُسْتَوْدَعَهَاؕ كُلٌّ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ مُّبِيْنٍ‏(6)\nWA MAA MIN DAABBATINW WA FIL ARZE ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE REZQUHAA WA YA’LAMO MUSTAQARRAHAA WAMUSTAWDAA’AHAA KULLUL FEE KETAABIM MOBEEN.\nThere is no moving creature on earth but its sustenance dependeth on Allah: He knoweth the time and place of its definite abode and its temporary deposit: All is in a clear Record. \nوَ هُوَ الَّذِىْ خَلَقَ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَ يَّامٍ وَّكَانَ عَرْشُهٗ عَلَى الْمَآءِ لِيَبْلُوَكُمْ اَيُّكُمْ اَحْسَنُ عَمَلًا ؕ وَلَئِنْ قُلْتَ اِنَّكُمْ مَّبْعُوْثُوْنَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِ الْمَوْتِ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذَاۤ اِلَّا سِحْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌ‏(7)\nWA HOWA LAZEE KHALAQAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA FEE SETTATE A’ZAABAN YYAAMIN WA KAANA A’ARSHUH A’LAL AL-MAAE LE-YABLOWAKUM AYYOKUM AHSANO A’AMALAN WA LAIN QULTA INNAKUM MAB-O’OSOONA MIN BA’DE MAWT LAYAQOOLANNA LAZEENA KAFAROO IN HAAZAA ILLAA SEHRUM MOBEEN.\nHe it is Who created the heavens and the earth in six Days - and His Throne was over the waters - that He might try you, which of you is best in conduct. But if thou wert to say to them, “Ye shall indeed be raised up after death”, the Unbelievers would be sure to say, “This is nothing but obvious sorcery!” \nوَلَئِنْ اَخَّرْنَا عَنْهُمُ الْعَذَابَ اِلٰٓى اُمَّةٍ مَّعْدُوْدَةٍ لَّيَقُوْلُنَّ مَا يَحْبِسُهٗؕ اَلَا يَوْمَ يَاْتِيْهِمْ لَيْسَ مَصْرُوْفًا عَنْهُمْ وَحَاقَ بِهِمْ مَّا كَانُوْا بِهٖ يَسْتَهْزِءُوْنَ‏(8)\nWA LAIN AAKKHARNAA A’NHOMUL A’ZAABA ELAA UMMATIN MMAA’DOODATIN LLAYAQOOLUNNA MAA YAHBESUH ALAA YAWMA YAATEEHIM LAYSA MASROOFAN A’NHUM WAHAAQA BEHIM MAA KAANOO BEHI YASTAHZEOON.\nIf We delay the penalty for them for a definite term, they are sure to say, “What keeps it back?” Ah! On the day it (actually) reaches them, nothing will turn it away from them, and they will be completely encircled by that which they used to mock at! \nوَلَئِنْ اَذَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ مِنَّا رَحْمَةً ثُمَّ نَزَعْنٰهَا مِنْهُۚ اِنَّهٗ لَيَئُوْسٌ كَفُوْرٌ‏(9)\nWA LAIN AZAQNAN INSAANA MINNAA RAHMATAM SUMMA NAZAA’NAAHAA MINHO INNAHU LAYAOOSUN KAFOORUN.\nIf We give man a taste of Mercy from Ourselves, and then withdraw it from him, behold! he is in despair and (falls into) blasphemy. \nوَلَئِنْ اَذَقْنٰهُ نَعْمَآءَ بَعْدَ ضَرَّآءَ مَسَّتْهُ لَيَقُوْلَنَّ ذَهَبَ السَّيِّاٰتُ عَنِّىْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَفَرِحٌ فَخُوْرٌۙ‏(10)\nWA LAIN AZAQNAAHO NAA’MAAA BA’DA ZARAAA-A MASSATHO LAYAQOOLANNA ZAHABAL AS-SAYAAATU A’NNEE INNAHU LAFAREHUN FAKHOORUN.\nBut if We give him a taste of (Our) favours after adversity hath touched him, he is sure to say, “All evil has departed from me:” Behold! he falls into exultation and pride. \nاِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ صَبَرُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمْ مَّغْفِرَةٌ وَّاَجْرٌ كَبِيْرٌ‏(11)\nILLAA LAZEENA SABAROO WA A’MELUS AS-SAALEHAATE OOLAAA-EKA LAHUM MAGHFERATUNW WA AJRUN KABEER.\nNot so do those who show patience and constancy, and work righteousness; for them is forgiveness (of sins) and a great reward. \nفَلَعَلَّكَ تَارِكٌۢ بَعْضَ مَا يُوْحٰٓى اِلَيْكَ وَضَآئِقٌ ۢ بِهٖ صَدْرُكَ اَنْ يَّقُوْلُوْا لَوْلَاۤ اُنْزِلَ عَلَيْهِ كَنْزٌ اَوْ جَآءَ مَعَهٗ مَلَكٌ ؕ اِنَّمَاۤ اَنْتَ نَذِيْرٌ ؕ وَاللّٰهُ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَّكِيْلٌ ؕ‏(12)\nFALAA’ALLAKA TAAREKUN YAWM MAA YOOHAA ELAYKA WAZAAEQUN BEHI SADRUKA AN YAQOOLOO LAWLAA UNZELA A’LAYHE KANZUN AW JAAA-A MA-A’HU MALAKUN INNAMAA ANTA NAZEERUM WAL LAAHO A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN WWAKEELUN.\nPerchance thou mayest (feel the inclination) to give up a part of what is revealed unto thee, and thy heart feeleth straitened lest they say, “Why is not a treasure sent down unto him, or why does not an angel come down with him?” But thou art there only to warn! It is Allah that arrangeth all affairs! \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ فَاْتُوْا بِعَشْرِ سُوَرٍ مِّثْلِهٖ مُفْتَرَيٰتٍ وَّ ادْعُوْا مَنِ اسْتَطَعْتُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ صٰدِقِيْنَ‏(13)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU QUL FAATOO BEA’ASHRE SOORIN MISLEH MUFTARAYTIN WA O’O MANIS ENIS TA-TA’TUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE IN KUNTUM SAADEQEEN.\nOr they may say, “He forged it,” Say, “Bring ye then ten suras forged, like unto it, and call (to your aid) whomsoever ye can, other than Allah!- If ye speak the truth! \nفَاِلَّمْ يَسْتَجِيْبُوْا لَكُمْ فَاعْلَمُوْۤا اَنَّمَاۤ اُنْزِلَ بِعِلْمِ اللّٰهِ وَاَنْ لَّاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَۚ فَهَلْ اَنْتُمْ مُّسْلِمُوْنَ‏(14)\nFAALLAM YASTAJEEBOO LAKUM FAAA’LAMOOA ANNAMAA UNZELA BEE’ELME LAAHE WA LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA FA HAL ANTUM MUSLEMOON.\n“If then they (your false gods) answer not your (call), know ye that this revelation is sent down (replete) with the knowledge of Allah, and that there is no god but He! will ye even then submit (to Islam)?” \nمَنْ كَانَ يُرِيْدُ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا وَ زِيْنَتَهَا نُوَفِّ اِلَيْهِمْ اَعْمَالَهُمْ فِيْهَا وَهُمْ فِيْهَا لَا يُبْخَسُوْنَ‏(15)\nMAN KAANA YOREEDO HAYAATAD DUNYAA WA ZEENATAHAA NOOFFE ELAYHIM A-A’MAALAHUM FEEHAA WA HUM FEEHAA LAA YUBKHASOONA.\nThose who desire the life of the present and its glitter, to them we shall pay (the price of) their deeds therein, without diminution. \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ لَيْسَ لَهُمْ فِىْ الْاٰخِرَةِ اِلَّا النَّارُ ۖ  وَحَبِطَ مَا صَنَعُوْا فِيْهَا وَبٰطِلٌ مَّا كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA LAYSA LAHUM FEE AAKHERATE ILLAA TAMASSANAN WAHABETA MAA SANAU’OOA FEEHAA WABAATELUN MAA KAANOO YA’MALOON.\nThey are those for whom there is nothing in the Hereafter but the Fire: vain are the designs they frame therein, and of no effect and the deeds that they do! \nاَفَمَنْ كَانَ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ وَيَتْلُوْهُ شَاهِدٌ مِّنْهُ وَمِنْ قَبْلِهٖ كِتٰبُ مُوْسٰٓى اِمَامًا وَّرَحْمَةً  ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُؤْمِنُوْنَ بِهٖ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّكْفُرْ بِهٖ مِنَ الْاَحْزَابِ فَالنَّارُ مَوْعِدُهٗ ۚ فَلَا تَكُ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّنْهُ اِنَّهُ الْحَقُّ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَ النَّاسِ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ‏(17)\nAFAMAWN KAANA A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN RABBEHI WAYATLOOHU SHAAHEDUN MINHO WA MIN QABLEHI KETAABU MOOSAA AEMAAMAN WA RAHMATAL OOLAAA-EKA YOAMENOONA BEHI WA MAN YAKFUR BEHI MENAL AL-AAHZAABE FANNAARO MAWE’EDUH FALAA TAKU FEE MIRYATIM MINHO INNAHUL HAQQO MIN RABBEKA LAAKINNAL AKSARAN NAASE LAA YOAMENOONA.\nCan they be (like) those who accept a Clear (Sign) from their Lord, and whom a witness from Himself doth teach, as did the Book of Moses before it, a guide and a mercy? They believe therein; but those of the Sects that reject it, the Fire will be their promised meeting-place. Be not then in doubt thereon: for it is the truth from thy Lord: yet many among men do not believe! \nوَمَنْ اَظْلَمُ مِمَّنِ افْتَرٰى عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا ؕ اُولٰٓئِكَ يُعْرَضُوْنَ عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ وَ يَقُوْلُ الْاَشْهَادُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ الَّذِيْنَ كَذَبُوْا عَلٰى رَبِّهِمْ ۚ اَلَا لَعْنَةُ اللّٰهِ عَلَى الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(18)\nWA MAN AZLAMO MIMMANIF TARAA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN OOLAAA-EKA YUA’RAZOONA A’LAA RABBEHIM WA YAQOOLO AL-AASHHAADU HAAOOLAAA-E LAZEENA KAZABOOA A’LAA RABBEHIM ALAA LA’NATUL LAAHE A’LAL ZAALEMEEN.\nWho doth more wrong than those who invent a life against Allah? They will be turned back to the presence of their Lord, and the witnesses will say, “These are the ones who lied against their Lord! Behold! the Curse of Allah is on those who do wrong!- \nالَّذِيْنَ يَصُدُّوْنَ عَنْ سَبِيْلِ اللّٰهِ وَيَبْغُوْنَهَا عِوَجًا ؕ وَهُمْ بِالْاٰخِرَةِ هُمْ كٰفِرُوْنَ‏(19)\nLAZEENA YASUDDOONA A’N SABEELIL LAAHE WAYABGHOONAHAA E’EWAJAN WA HUM BIL AAKHERATE HUM KAAFEROON.\n“Those who would hinder (men) from the path of Allah and would seek in it something crooked: these were they who denied the Hereafter!” \nاُولٰٓئِكَ لَمْ يَكُوْنُوْا مُعْجِزِيْنَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا كَانَ لَهُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ ۘ يُضٰعَفُ لَهُمُ الْعَذَابُ ؕ مَا كَانُوْا يَسْتَطِيْعُوْنَ السَّمْعَ وَمَا كَانُوْا يُبْصِرُوْنَ‏(20)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAM YAKOONOOA MUA’JEZEENA FIL ARZE WA MAA KAANA LAHUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN AAWLEEAAAA YUZAAA’AFU LAHOMUL A’ZAABO MAA KAANOO YASTATEE-O’ONA JA-A’LA WA MAA KAANOO YUBSEROON.\nThey will in no wise frustrate (His design) on earth, nor have they protectors besides Allah! Their penalty will be doubled! They lost the power to hear, and they did not see! \nاُولٰٓئِكَ الَّذِيْنَ خَسِرُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ وَضَلَّ عَنْهُمْ مَّا كَانُوْا يَفْتَرُوْنَ‏(21)\nOOLAAA-EKA LAZEENA KHASEROOA ANFOSAHUM WA ZALLA A’NHUM MAA KAANOO YAFTAROON.\nThey are the ones who have lost their own souls: and the (fancies) they invented have left them in the lurch! \nلَا جَرَمَ اَ نَّهُمْ فِى الْاٰخِرَةِ هُمُ الْاَخْسَرُوْنَ‏(22)\nLAA JARAMA A’ZAABAN NNAHUM FIL AAKHERATE HOMUL AKHSAROON.\nWithout a doubt, these are the very ones who will lose most in the Hereafter! \nاِنَّ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَعَمِلُوا الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَاَخْبَتُوْۤا اِلٰى رَبِّهِمْۙ اُولٰٓئِكَ اَصْحٰبُ الْجَنَّةِؕ هُمْ فِيْهَا خٰلِدُوْنَ‏(23)\nINNAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WA A’MELUS SAALEHAATE WAAKHBATOOA ELAA RABBEHIM OOLAAA-EKA ASHAABUN JANNAH HUM FEEHAA KHAALEDOON.\nBut those who believe and work righteousness, and humble themselves before their Lord, They will be companions of the gardens, to dwell therein for aye! \nمَثَلُ الْفَرِيْقَيْنِ كَالْاَعْمٰى وَالْاَصَمِّ وَالْبَصِيْرِ وَالسَّمِيْعِ ؕ هَلْ يَسْتَوِيٰنِ مَثَلًا ؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(24)\nMASALUL AL-FAREEQAYNE KA-A-A’MAA WAL AASAMME WAL BASEERE WAALSSAMEEE’E HAL YASTAWEENE MASALAA AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\nThese two kinds (of men) may be compared to the blind and deaf, and those who can see and hear well. Are they equal when compared? Will ye not then take heed? \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا نُوْحًا اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖۤ اِنِّىْ لَكُمْ نَذِيْرٌ مُّبِيْنٌۙ‏(25)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA ARSALNAA ELAA QAWMEHI INNEE LAKUM NAZEERUM MOBEEN.\nWe sent Noah to his people (with a mission): “I have come to you with a Clear Warning: \nاَنْ لَّا تَعْبُدُوْۤا اِلَّا اللّٰهَؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ اَلِيْمٍ‏(26)\nAN LAA TA’BODOO ILLAA LAAH INNEE AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN ALEEM.\n“That ye serve none but Allah: Verily I do fear for you the penalty of a grievous day.” \nفَقَالَ الْمَلَاُ الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا مِنْ قَوْمِهٖ مَا نَرٰٮكَ اِلَّا بَشَرًا مِّثْلَنَا وَمَا نَرٰٮكَ اتَّبَعَكَ اِلَّا الَّذِيْنَ هُمْ اَرَاذِلُنَا بَادِىَ الرَّاْىِۚ وَمَا نَرٰى لَكُمْ عَلَيْنَا مِنْ فَضْلٍۢ بَلْ نَظُنُّكُمْ كٰذِبِيْنَ‏(27)\nFAQAALA MALA-O LAZEENA KAFAROO MIN QAWMEHI MAA NARAAKA ILLAA BASHARAN MMESLANAA WA MAA NARAAKA ATTABAA’AKA ILLAA LAZEENA HUM AARAAZELUNAA BAADEAAA AR-RAAAAE WA MAA NARAA LAKUM A’LAYNAA MIN FAZLIN BAL NAZUNNUKUM KAAZEBEENA.\nBut the chiefs of the Unbelievers among his people said: “We see (in) thee nothing but a man like ourselves: Nor do we see that any follow thee but the meanest among us, in judgment immature: Nor do we see in you (all) any merit above us: in fact we thing ye are liars!” \nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاٰتٰٮنِىْ رَحْمَةً مِّنْ عِنْدِهٖ فَعُمِّيَتْ عَلَيْكُمْؕ اَنُلْزِمُكُمُوْهَا وَاَنْتُمْ لَهَا كٰرِهُوْنَ‏(28)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WAATAANEAA RAHMATAM MIN I’NDEHI FAU’UMMEET A’LAYKUM AANULZEMUKUMOOHAA WA ANTUM LAHAA KAAREHOONA.\nHe said: “O my people! See ye if (it be that) I have a Clear Sign from my Lord, and that He hath sent Mercy unto me from His own presence, but that the Mercy hath been obscured from your sight? shall we compel you to accept it when ye are averse to it? \nوَيٰقَوْمِ لَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ مَالًا ؕاِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى اللّٰهِ وَمَاۤ اَنَا بِطَارِدِ الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا ؕ اِنَّهُمْ مُّلٰقُوْا رَبِّهِمْ وَلٰكِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ قَوْمًا تَجْهَلُوْنَ‏(29)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE MAALAWN AEN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAAHE WA MAA ANAA BETAAREDE LAZEENA AAMANOO INNAHUM MOLAAQOO RABBEHIM WALAAKENNEAA AARAAKUM QAWMAN TAJHALOON.\n“And O my people! I ask you for no wealth in return: my reward is from none but Allah: But I will not drive away (in contempt) those who believe: for verily they are to meet their Lord, and ye I see are the ignorant ones! \nوَيٰقَوْمِ مَنْ يَّنْصُرُنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ طَرَدتُّهُمْؕ اَفَلَا تَذَكَّرُوْنَ‏(30)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI MAN YYANSURUNEAA MENAL LAAHE IN TARADTTUHUM AFALAA TAZAKKAROON.\n“And O my people! who would help me against Allah if I drove them away? Will ye not then take heed? \nوَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لَكُمْ عِنْدِىْ خَزَآئِنُ اللّٰهِ وَلَاۤ اَعْلَمُ الْغَيْبَ وَلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ اِنِّىْ مَلَكٌ وَّلَاۤ اَقُوْلُ لِلَّذِيْنَ تَزْدَرِىْۤ اَعْيُنُكُمْ لَنْ يُّؤْتِيَهُمُ اللّٰهُ خَيْرًا ؕ اَللّٰهُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا فِىْۤ اَنْفُسِهِمْ ۖۚ اِنِّىْۤ اِذًا لَّمِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(31)\nWA LAA AAQOOLU LAKUM E’ENDEAA KHAZAAENUS LAAHE WA LAA A-A’LAMO GHAYBA WA LAA AAQOOLU INNEE MALAKUN WA LAA AAQOOLU LILLAZEENA TAZDAREAA AAA’YUNUKUM LAN YYUTEEHUMU LAAHO KHAYRAN ALLAAHO A-A’LAMO BEMAA FEE ANFOSEHIM INNEE EZAL LAMENAZ ZAALEMEEN.\n“I tell you not that with me are the treasures of Allah, nor do I know what is hidden, nor claim I to be an angel. Nor yet do I say, of those whom your eyes do despise that Allah will not grant them (all) that is good: Allah knoweth best what is in their souls: I should, if I did, indeed be a wrong-doer.” \nقَالُوْا يٰنُوْحُ قَدْ جَادَلْتَنَا فَاَكْثَرْتَ جِدَالَنَا فَاْتِنَا بِمَا تَعِدُنَاۤ اِنْ كُنْتَ مِنَ الصّٰدِقِيْنَ‏ ‏(32)\nQAALOO YAANOOHU QAD JAADALTANAA FAAKSARTA JEDAALANAA FAATENAA BEMAA TAE’EDUNAA IN KUNTA MENAL SAADEQEENA.\nThey said: “O Noah! thou hast disputed with us, and (much) hast thou prolonged the dispute with us: now bring upon us what thou threatenest us with, if thou speakest the truth!?” \nقَالَ اِنَّمَا يَاْتِيْكُمْ بِهِ اللّٰهُ اِنْ شَآءَ وَمَاۤ اَنْتُمْ بِمُعْجِزِيْنَ‏(33)\nQAALA INNAMAA YAATEEKUM BEHIL LAAHO IN SHAAA-AL WA MAA ANTUM BE-MO’JEZEENA.\nHe said: “Truly, Allah will bring it on you if He wills, and then, ye will not be able to frustrate it! \nوَلَا يَنْفَعُكُمْ نُصْحِىْۤ اِنْ اَرَدْتُّ اَنْ اَنْصَحَ لَكُمْ اِنْ كَانَ اللّٰهُ يُرِيْدُ اَنْ يُّغْوِيَكُمْؕ هُوَ رَبُّكُمْ وَاِلَيْهِ تُرْجَعُوْنَؕ‏(34)\nWA LAA YANFAU’UKUM NUSHEAA IN AARADTTU AN AANSAHA LAKUM IN KAANA LAAHO YOREEDO AN YYUGHWEEKUM HOWA RABBOKUM WA ELAYHE TURJAU’OONA.\n“Of no profit will be my counsel to you, much as I desire to give you (good) counsel, if it be that Allah willeth to leave you astray: He is your Lord! and to Him will ye return!” \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ افْتَرٰٮهُ ؕ قُلْ اِنِ افْتَرَيْتُهٗ فَعَلَىَّ اِجْرَامِىْ وَاَنَا بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُجْرِمُوْنَ‏(35)\nAM YAQOOLOONA AFTARAAHU QUL ENIS AFTARAYTUH FA A’LAYYA AEJRAAMEAA ANAT BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUJREMOONA.\nOr do they say, “He has forged it”? Say: “If I had forged it, on me were my sin! and I am free of the sins of which ye are guilty! \nوَاُوْحِىَ اِلٰى نُوْحٍ اَنَّهٗ لَنْ يُّؤْمِنَ مِنْ قَوْمِكَ اِلَّا مَنْ قَدْ اٰمَنَ فَلَا تَبْتَئِسْ بِمَا كَانُوْا يَفْعَلُوْنَ ۖ  ۚ‏(36)\nWA OOHEYA ELAA NOOHIN ANNAHU LAN YYUMENA MIN QAWMEKA ILLAA MAN QAD AAMANA FALAA TABTAES BEMAA KAANOO YAF-A’LOON.\nIt was revealed to Noah: “None of thy people will believe except those who have believed already! So grieve no longer over their (evil) deeds. \nوَاصْنَعِ الْفُلْكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَوَحْيِنَا وَلَا تُخَاطِبْنِىْ فِى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا ۚ اِنَّهُمْ مُّغْرَقُوْنَ‏(37)\nWAASNAE’E AL-FULKA BEAAA’YUNENAA WAWAHYENAA WA LAA TUKHAATEBNEAA FIL LAZEENA ZALAMOO INNAHUM MUGHRAQOON.\n“But construct an Ark under Our eyes and Our inspiration, and address Me no (further) on behalf of those who are in sin: for they are about to be overwhelmed (in the Flood).” \nوَيَصْنَعُ الْفُلْكَ وَكُلَّمَا مَرَّ عَلَيْهِ مَلَاٌ مِّنْ قَوْمِهٖ سَخِرُوْا مِنْهُؕ قَالَ اِنْ تَسْخَرُوْا مِنَّا فَاِنَّا نَسْخَرُ مِنْكُمْ كَمَا تَسْخَرُوْنَؕ‏(38)\nWAYASNAU’U AL-FULKA WA KULLAMAA MARRA A’LAYHE MALAA MIN QAWMEHI SAKHEROOA MENHU QAALA IN TASKHAROOA MINNAA FAINNAA NASKHARU MINKUM KAMAA TASKHAROONA.\nForthwith he (starts) constructing the Ark: Every time that the chiefs of his people passed by him, they threw ridicule on him. He said: “If ye ridicule us now, we (in our turn) can look down on you with ridicule likewise! \nفَسَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَۙ مَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَيَحِلُّ عَلَيْهِ عَذَابٌ مُّقِيْمٌ‏(39)\nFA-SAWFA TA’LAMOON MAN YYAATEEHE A’ZAABUN YYUKHZEEHE WA YAHILLO A’LAYHE A’ZAABUN MMUQEEMUN.\n“But soon will ye know who it is on whom will descend a penalty that will cover them with shame, on whom will be unloosed a penalty lasting:” \nحَتّٰۤى اِذَا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا وَفَارَ التَّنُّوْرُۙ قُلْنَا احْمِلْ فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلٍّ زَوْجَيْنِ اثْنَيْنِ وَاَهْلَكَ اِلَّا مَنْ سَبَقَ عَلَيْهِ الْقَوْلُ وَمَنْ اٰمَنَؕ وَمَاۤ اٰمَنَ مَعَهٗۤ اِلَّا قَلِيْلٌ‏(40)\nHATTAA EZAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA WAFAARA AT-TANNOORU QULNAL AHMEL FEEHAA MIN KULLIN ZAWJAYNE NAYNE WA AHLAKA ILLAA MAN SABAQA A’LAYHE QAWLO WA MAN AAAMANA WA MAA AAMANA MA-A’HU ILLAA QALEELUN.\nAt length, behold! there came Our command, and the fountains of the earth gushed forth! We said: “Embark therein, of each kind two, male and female, and your family - except those against whom the word has already gone forth, and the Believers.” but only a few believed with him. \nوَقَالَ ارْكَبُوْا فِيْهَا بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ مَجْرٖؔٮٰھَا وَمُرْسٰٮهَا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ لَغَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ ‏(41)\nWA QAALA ARKABOOA FEEHAA BISMIL LAAHE MAJRA WAMURSAAHAA INNAL RABBEE LAGHAFOORUN RAHEEM.\nSo he said: “Embark ye on the Ark, In the name of Allah, whether it move or be at rest! For my Lord is, be sure, Oft-Forgiving, Most Merciful!” \nوَهِىَ تَجْرِىْ بِهِمْ فِىْ مَوْجٍ كَالْجِبَالِ وَنَادٰى نُوْحُ اۨبْنَهٗ وَكَانَ فِىْ مَعْزِلٍ يّٰبُنَىَّ ارْكَبْ مَّعَنَا وَلَا تَكُنْ مَّعَ الْكٰفِرِيْنَ‏(42)\nWA HEYA TAJREE BEHIM FEE MAWJIN KA-JEBAALE WANAADAA NOOHU ABNAH KAANAL FEE MAA’ZELIN YYAABUNAA ARKAB MMAA’ANAA WA LAA TAKUN MA-A’L KAAFEREEN.\nSo the Ark floated with them on the waves (towering) like mountains, and Noah called out to his son, who had separated himself (from the rest): “O my son! embark with us, and be not with the unbelievers!” \nقَالَ سَاٰوِىْۤ اِلٰى جَبَلٍ يَّعْصِمُنِىْ مِنَ الْمَآءِؕ قَالَ لَا عَاصِمَ الْيَوْمَ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِ اِلَّا مَنْ رَّحِمَۚ وَحَالَ بَيْنَهُمَا الْمَوْجُ فَكَانَ مِنَ الْمُغْرَقِيْنَ‏(43)\nQAALA SAAWEAA ELAA JABALIM YYAA’SEMUNEAA MENAL AL-MAAE QAALA LAA A’AASEMA YAWMA MIN AMRE LAAHE ILLAA MAN RAHEMAL WAHAALA BAYNAHOMAA AL-MAWJU FA KAANA MENAL AL-MUGHRAQEENA.\nThe son replied: “I will betake myself to some mountain: it will save me from the water.” Noah said: “This day nothing can save, from the command of Allah, any but those on whom He hath mercy! “And the waves came between them, and the son was among those overwhelmed in the Flood. \nوَقِيْلَ يٰۤاَرْضُ ابْلَعِىْ مَآءَكِ وَيٰسَمَآءُ اَقْلِعِىْ وَغِيْضَ الْمَآءُ وَقُضِىَ الْاَمْرُ وَاسْتَوَتْ عَلَى الْجُوْدِىِّ وَقِيْلَ بُعْدًا لِّلْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ‏(44)\nWA QEELAD YAARZU ABLAE’EAA MAAAKE WAYSAMAAU AAQLEE’EAA WAGHEEZA AL-MAAU WA MIN WAASTAWAT A’LAL AL-JOODEAAAE WA QEELAD BUA’DAN LLELQAWME ZAALEMEEN.\nThen the word went forth: “O earth! swallow up thy water, and O sky! Withhold (thy rain)!” and the water abated, and the matter was ended. The Ark rested on Mount Judi, and the word went forth: “Away with those who do wrong!” \nوَنَادٰى نُوْحٌ رَّبَّهٗ فَقَالَ رَبِّ اِنَّ ابْنِىْ مِنْ اَهْلِىْ وَاِنَّ وَعْدَكَ الْحَقُّ وَاَنْتَ اَحْكَمُ الْحٰكِمِيْنَ‏(45)\nWANAADAA NOOHUN RRABBAH FAQAALA RABBE INNAL ABNEAA MIN AAHLEAA WA INNA WAA’DAKA HAQQO WA ANTA AAHKAMU HAAKEMEEN.\nAnd Noah called upon his Lord, and said: “O my Lord! surely my son is of my family! and Thy promise is true, and Thou art the justest of Judges!” \nقَالَ يٰنُوْحُ اِنَّهٗ لَيْسَ مِنْ اَهْلِكَ ۚاِنَّهٗ عَمَلٌ غَيْرُ صَالِحٍ ۖ فَلَا تَسْئَلْنِ مَا لَيْسَ لَكَ بِهٖ عِلْمٌ ؕ اِنِّىْۤ اَعِظُكَ اَنْ تَكُوْنَ مِنَ الْجٰهِلِيْنَ‏(46)\nQAALA YAANOOHU INNAHU LAYSA MIN AAHLEKA INNAHU A’AMALUN GHAYRO SAALEHIN FALAA TASALNE MAA LAYSA LAKA BEHI I’LMUM INNEE AAE’EZUKA AN TAKOONA MENAL JAAHELEEN.\nHe said: “O Noah! He is not of thy family: For his conduct is unrighteous. So ask not of Me that of which thou hast no knowledge! I give thee counsel, lest thou act like the ignorant!” \nقَالَ رَبِّ اِنِّىْۤ اَعُوْذُ بِكَ اَنْ اَسْئَلَكَ مَا لَيْسَ لِىْ بِهٖ عِلْمٌؕ وَاِلَّا تَغْفِرْ لِىْ وَتَرْحَمْنِىْۤ اَكُنْ مِّنَ الْخٰسِرِيْنَ‏(47)\nQAALA RABBE INNEE A-OO’ZO BEKA AN AASALAKA MAA LAYSA LEE BEHI E’ELMUN WA ILLAA TAGHFER LEE WATARHAMNEAA AAKUN MENAL KHAASEREEN.\nNoah said: “O my Lord! I do seek refuge with Thee, lest I ask Thee for that of which I have no knowledge. And unless thou forgive me and have Mercy on me, I should indeed be lost!” \nقِيْلَ يٰنُوْحُ اهْبِطْ بِسَلٰمٍ مِّنَّا وَبَرَكٰتٍ عَلَيْكَ وَعَلٰٓى اُمَمٍ مِّمَّنْ مَّعَكَؕ وَاُمَمٌ سَنُمَتِّعُهُمْ ثُمَّ يَمَسُّهُمْ مِّنَّا عَذَابٌ اَلِيْمٌ‏(48)\nQEELA YAANOOHU AHBET BESALAAMIN MINNAA WABARAKAATIN A’LAYKA WA A’LAA OMAMIN MIMMAYN MMAA’AKA WA OMAMUM SANUMATTEU’UHUM SUMMA YAMASSUHUM MINNAA A’ZAABUN ALEEM.\nThe word came: “O Noah! Come down (from the Ark) with peace from Us, and blessing on thee and on some of the peoples (who will spring) from those with thee: but (there will be other) peoples to whom We shall grant their pleasures (for a time), but in the end will a grievous penalty reach them from Us.” \nتِلْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْغَيْبِ نُوْحِيْهَاۤ اِلَيْكَۚ مَا كُنْتَ تَعْلَمُهَاۤ اَنْتَ وَلَا قَوْمُكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ هٰذَا ۛؕ فَاصْبِرْ ۛؕ اِنَّ الْعَاقِبَةَ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ‏(49)\nTILKA MIN AANBAAE GHAYBE NOOHEEHAA ELAYKA MAA KUNTA TAA’LAMUHAA ANTA WA LAA QAWMUKA MIN QABLE HAAZAA FAS-BIR INNAL AL-A’AAQEBATA LILMUTTAQEEN.\nSuch are some of the stories of the unseen, which We have revealed unto thee: before this, neither thou nor thy people knew them. So persevere patiently: for the End is for those who are righteous. \nوَاِلٰى عَادٍ اَخَاهُمْ هُوْدًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ اِنْ اَنْتُمْ اِلَّا مُفْتَرُوْنَ‏(50)\nWA ELAA A’ADIN SAMOODA HOODAN QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH IN ANTUM ILLAA MUFTAROONA.\nTo the 'Ad People (We sent) Hud, one of their own brethren. He said: “O my people! worship Allah! ye have no other god but Him. (Your other gods) ye do nothing but invent! \nيٰقَوْمِ لَاۤ اَسْئَلُكُمْ عَلَيْهِ اَجْرًا ؕ اِنْ اَجْرِىَ اِلَّا عَلَى الَّذِىْ فَطَرَنِىْ ؕ اَفَلَا تَعْقِلُوْنَ‏(51)\nLE-QAWMEHI LAA AASALUKUM A’LAYHE AJRAN IN AAJREAAA ILLAA A’LAL LAZEE FATARANEE AFALAA TA’QELOON.\n“O my people! I ask of you no reward for this (Message). My reward is from none but Him who created me: Will ye not then understand? \nوَيٰقَوْمِ اسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ يُرْسِلِ السَّمَآءَ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّدْرَارًا وَّيَزِدْكُمْ قُوَّةً اِلٰى قُوَّتِكُمْ وَلَا تَتَوَلَّوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(52)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI ASTAGHFEROOA TAQUL SUMMA TOOBOOA ELAYHE YURSELE SAMAAA-AD A’LAYKUM MMEDRAARAN WWAYAZEDKUM QUWWAH ELAA QOOTEKUM WA LAA IN MUJREMEEN.\n“And O my people! Ask forgiveness of your Lord, and turn to Him (in repentance): He will send you the skies pouring abundant rain, and add strength to your strength: so turn ye not back in sin!” \nقَالُوْا يٰهُوْدُ مَا جِئْتَنَا بِبَيِّنَةٍ وَّمَا نَحْنُ بِتٰرِكِىْۤ اٰلِهَتِنَا عَنْ قَوْلِكَ وَمَا نَحْنُ لَكَ بِمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(53)\nQAALOO YAAHOODU MAA JETANAA BE-BAYYENAH WA MAA NAHNO BETAAREKEAA AAALEHATENAA A’N QAWLEKA WA MAA NAHNO LAKA BE-MOAMENEEN.\nThey said: “O Hud! No Clear (Sign) that hast thou brought us, and we are not the ones to desert our gods on thy word! Nor shall we believe in thee! \nاِنْ نَّقُوْلُ اِلَّا اعْتَرٰٮكَ بَعْضُ اٰلِهَتِنَا بِسُوْٓءٍ ؕ قَالَ اِنِّىْۤ اُشْهِدُ اللّٰهَ وَاشْهَدُوْۤا اَنِّىْ بَرِىْٓءٌ مِّمَّا تُشْرِكُوْنَ ۙ‏(54)\nIN NNAQOOLU ILLAA AA’TARAAKA BA’ZUL AAALEHATENAA BE-SOOO-IN QAALA INNEE AUSHHEDU LAAHA WAASHHADOOA AANNEAA BAREEE-UM MIMMAA TUSHREKOONA.\n“We say nothing but that (perhaps) some of our gods may have seized thee with imbecility.” He said: “I call Allah to witness, and do ye bear witness, that I am free from the sin of ascribing, to Him, \nمِنْ دُوْنِهٖ فَكِيْدُوْنِىْ جَمِيْعًا ثُمَّ لَا تُنْظِرُوْنِ‏(55)\nMIN DOONEHI FAKEEDOONEAA JAMEE-A’A SUMMA LAA TUNZEROONE.\n“Other gods as partners! so scheme (your worst) against me, all of you, and give me no respite. \nاِنِّىْ تَوَكَّلْتُ عَلَى اللّٰهِ رَبِّىْ وَرَبِّكُمْ ؕ مَا مِنْ دَآبَّةٍ اِلَّا هُوَ اٰخِذٌ ۢ بِنَاصِيَتِهَا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ عَلٰى صِرَاطٍ مُّسْتَقِيْمٍ‏(56)\nINNEE TAWAKKALTU A’LAL LAAHE RABBEE WA RABBEKUM MAA MIN DAAAB-BATIL ILLAA HOWA AAAKHEZUN BENAASEETEHAA INNAL RABBEE A’LAA SERAATIM MUSTAQEEM.\n“I put my trust in Allah, My Lord and your Lord! There is not a moving creature, but He hath grasp of its fore-lock. Verily, it is my Lord that is on a straight Path. \nفَاِنْ تَوَلَّوْا فَقَدْ اَبْلَغْتُكُمْ مَّاۤ اُرْسِلْتُ بِهٖۤ اِلَيْكُمْ ؕ وَيَسْتَخْلِفُ رَبِّىْ قَوْمًا غَيْرَكُمْۚ وَلَا تَضُرُّوْنَهٗ شَيْئًا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ حَفِيْظٌ‏(57)\nFA-IN TAWALLAW FAQAD AABLAGHTUKUM MAA AURSELTU BEHI ELAYKUM WAYASTAKHLEFU RABBEE QAWMAN GHAYRAKUM WA LAA TAZURROONAH SHAY-ANW INNAL RABBEE A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN HAFEEZUN.\n“If ye turn away, I (at least) have conveyed the Message with which I was sent to you. My Lord will make another people to succeed you, and you will not harm Him in the least. For my Lord hath care and watch over all things.” \nوَ لَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا هُوْدًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا ۚ وَ نَجَّيْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ عَذَابٍ غَلِيْظٍ‏(58)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA NAJJAYNAL HOODAN WWAALLAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BERAHMATIN MINNAA WA NAJJAYNAAHUM MIN A’ZAABIN GHALEEZ.\nSo when Our decree issued, We saved Hud and those who believed with him, by (special) Grace from Ourselves: We saved them from a severe penalty. \nوَتِلْكَ عَادٌ جَحَدُوْا بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَعَصَوْا رُسُلَهٗ وَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَمْرَ كُلِّ جَبَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍ‏(59)\nWA TILKAL A’ADUN JAHADOOA BE-AAYAATIL RABBEHIM WAA’ASAWA ROSOLAHU WAT TABA-O’O AAMRA KULLE JABBAARIN A’ANEEDIN.\nSuch were the 'Ad People: they rejected the Signs of their Lord and Cherisher; disobeyed His messengers; And followed the command of every powerful, obstinate transgressor. \nوَاُتْبِعُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهِ الدُّنْيَا لَعْنَةً وَّيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ عَادًا كَفَرُوْا رَبَّهُمْؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّعَادٍ قَوْمِ هُوْدٍ‏(60)\nWAATBEU’OOA FEE HAAZEHE DUNYAA LA’NAH WWAYAWMA AL-QEEMATE ALAA INNAL A’AADAN KAFAROO RABBAHUM ALAA BUA’DAN LLEA’AADIN QAWME HOODIN.\nAnd they were pursued by a Curse in this life, and on the Day of Judgment. Ah! Behold! for the 'Ad rejected their Lord and Cherisher! Ah! Behold! removed (from sight) were 'Ad the people of Hud! \nوَاِلٰى ثَمُوْدَ اَخَاهُمْ صٰلِحًاۘ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ هُوَ اَنْشَاَكُمْ مِّنَ الْاَرْضِ وَاسْتَعْمَرَكُمْ فِيْهَا فَاسْتَغْفِرُوْهُ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِ ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ قَرِيْبٌ مُّجِيْبٌ‏(61)\nWA ELAA ELAA SAMOODA AKHAAHUM QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH HOWA AN-SHA-A MENAL ARZE WAASTAA’MARAKUM FEEHAA FAASTAGHFEROOHU SUMMA TOOBOOA ELAYHE INNAL RABBEE QAREEB MMUJEEBUN.\nTo the Thamud People (We sent) Salih, one of their own brethren. He said: “O my people! Worship Allah: ye have no other god but Him. It is He Who hath produced you from the earth and settled you therein: then ask forgiveness of Him, and turn to Him (in repentance): for my Lord is (always) near, ready to answer.” \nقَالُوْا يٰصٰلِحُ قَدْ كُنْتَ فِيْنَا مَرْجُوًّا قَبْلَ هٰذَآ اَتَنْهٰٮنَاۤ اَنْ نَّعْبُدَ مَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَا وَاِنَّنَا لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّمَّا تَدْعُوْنَاۤ اِلَيْهِ مُرِيْبٍ‏(62)\nQAALOO YAASAALEHU QAD KUNTA FEENAA MARJOOA QABLA HAAZAA AATANHAANAA AN NNAA’BUDA MAA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUNAA WA INNANAA LAFEE SHAKKIM MIMMAA TAD-O’ONAA ELAYHE MOREEB.\nThey said: “O Salih! thou hast been of us! a centre of our hopes hitherto! dost thou (now) forbid us the worship of what our fathers worshipped? But we are really in suspicious (disquieting) doubt as to that to which thou invitest us.” \nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَاٰتٰٮنِىْ مِنْهُ رَحْمَةً فَمَنْ يَّنْصُرُنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اِنْ عَصَيْتُهٗ فَمَا تَزِيْدُوْنَنِىْ غَيْرَ تَخْسِيْرٍ‏(63)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WAATAANEAA MINHO RAHMATAM FAMAN YYANSURUNEAA MENAL LAAHE IN A’ASAYTUH FAMAA TAZEEDOONANEAA GHAYRA TAKHSEERIN.\nHe said: “O my people! do ye see? if I have a Clear (Sign) from my Lord and He hath sent Mercy unto me from Himself, who then can help me against Allah if I were to disobey Him? What then would ye add to my (portion) but perdition? \nوَيٰقَوْمِ هٰذِهٖ نَاقَةُ اللّٰهِ لَكُمْ اٰيَةً فَذَرُوْهَا تَاْكُلْ فِىْۤ اَرْضِ اللّٰهِ وَلَا تَمَسُّوْهَا بِسُوْٓءٍ فَيَاْخُذَكُمْ عَذَابٌ قَرِيْبٌ‏(64)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI HAAZEHI NAAQATU LAAHE LAKUM AAYATAL FAZAROOHAA TAAKUL FEE AARZE LAAHE WA LAA TAMASSOOHAA BE-SOOO-IN FAYAAKHUZAKUM A’ZAABUN QAREEB.\n“And O my people! This she-camel of Allah is a symbol to you: leave her to feed on Allah's (free) earth, and inflict no harm on her, or a swift penalty will seize you!” \nفَعَقَرُوْهَا فَقَالَ تَمَتَّعُوْا فِىْ دَارِكُمْ ثَلٰثَةَ اَ يَّامٍ ؕذٰ لِكَ وَعْدٌ غَيْرُ مَكْذُوْبٍ‏(65)\nFA-A’QAROOHAA FAQAALA TAMATTAU’OOA FEE DAAREKUM SALAASATA A’ZAABAN YYAAMIN ZAA LEKA WAA’DUN GHAYRO MAKZOOBIN.\nBut they did ham-string her. So he said: “Enjoy yourselves in your homes for three days: (Then will be your ruin): (Behold) there a promise not to be belied!” \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا صٰلِحًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا وَمِنْ خِزْىِ يَوْمِئِذٍؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ هُوَ الْقَوِىُّ الْعَزِيْزُ‏(66)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA NAJJAYNAL AKHAAHUM WWAALLAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BERAHMATIN MINNAA WA MIN KHEZAAE YAWMEEZIN INNAL RABBAKA HOWA QAWIYYUL A’ZEEZUL.\nWhen Our Decree issued, We saved Salih and those who believed with him, by (special) Grace from Ourselves - and from the Ignominy of that day. For thy Lord - He is the Strong One, and able to enforce His Will. \nوَاَخَذَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دِيَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَۙ‏(67)\nWAAKHAZA LAZEENA ZALAMOOA AS-SAYHATU FA-ASBAHOO FEE DEYAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nThe (mighty) Blast overtook the wrong-doers, and they lay prostrate in their homes before the morning, \nكَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ؕ اَلَاۤ اِنَّ ثَمُوْدَا۟ كَفَرُوْا رَبَّهُمْؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّثَمُوْدَ‏(68)\nKA-AN LAM YAGHNAWA FEEHAA ALAA INNAL SAMOODAA KAFAROO RABBAHUM ALAA BUA’DAN LLESAMOODA.\nAs if they had never dwelt and flourished there. Ah! Behold! for the Thamud rejected their Lord and Cherisher! Ah! Behold! removed (from sight) were the Thamud! \nوَلَقَدْ جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَاۤ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ بِالْبُشْرٰى قَالُوْا سَلٰمًا ؕ قَالَ سَلٰمٌ فَمَا لَبِثَ اَنْ جَآءَ بِعِجْلٍ حَنِيْذٍ‏(69)\nWA LAQAD JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA IBRAAHEEMA BIL-BUSHRAA QAALOO SALAAMAA QAALA SALAAMUN FAMAA LABESA AN JAAA-A BEE’EJLIN HANEEZIN.\nThere came Our messengers to Abraham with glad tidings. They said, “Peace!” He answered, “Peace!” and hastened to entertain them with a roasted calf. \nفَلَمَّا رَاٰۤ اَيْدِيَهُمْ لَا تَصِلُ اِلَيْهِ نَكِرَهُمْ وَاَوْجَسَ مِنْهُمْ خِيْفَةً  ؕ قَالُوْا لَا تَخَفْ اِنَّاۤ اُرْسِلْنَاۤ اِلٰى قَوْمِ لُوْطٍ ؕ‏(70)\nFALAMMAA RAA AYDEYAHUM LAA TASELU ELAYHE NAKERAHUM WAAWJASA MINHUM KHEEFATAN QAALOO LAA TAKHAF INNAA AURSELNAA ELAA QAWME LOOTIM.\nBut when he saw their hands went not towards the (meal), he felt some mistrust of them, and conceived a fear of them. They said: “Fear not: We have been sent against the people of Lut.” \nوَامْرَاَ تُهٗ قَآئِمَةٌ فَضَحِكَتْ فَبَشَّرْنٰهَا بِاِسْحٰقَ ۙ وَمِنْ وَّرَآءِ اِسْحٰقَ يَعْقُوْبَ‏(71)\nWAAMRAA RA-ATOHU QAAEMATUN FAZAHEKAT FABASSHARNAAHAA BE-ISHAAQA WA MIN FAS-ALOOHUNNA ISHAAQA YA’QOOBAL.\nAnd his wife was standing (there), and she laughed: But we gave her glad tidings of Isaac, and after him, of Jacob. \nقَالَتْ يٰوَيْلَتٰٓى ءَاَلِدُ وَاَنَا عَجُوْزٌ وَّهٰذَا بَعْلِىْ شَيْخًا ؕ اِنَّ هٰذَا لَشَىْءٌ عَجِيْبٌ‏(72)\nQAALAT YAAWAYLATAAA AALEDU ANAT A’AJOOZUN WWAHAAZAA BAA’LEAA SHAYKHAN INNAL HAAZAA LASHAAUN A’AJEEBUN.\nShe said: “Alas for me! shall I bear a child, seeing I am an old woman, and my husband here is an old man? That would indeed be a wonderful thing!” \nقَالُوْۤا اَتَعْجَبِيْنَ مِنْ اَمْرِ اللّٰهِ رَحْمَتُ اللّٰهِ وَبَرَكٰتُهٗ عَلَيْكُمْ اَهْلَ الْبَيْتِؕ اِنَّهٗ حَمِيْدٌ مَّجِيْدٌ‏(73)\nQAALOO AATAA’JABEENA MIN AMRE LAAHE RAHMATU LAAHE WABARAKAATUH A’LAYKUM AHLAL AL-BAYTE INNAHU HAMEED MAJEEDUN.\nThey said: “Dost thou wonder at Allah's decree? The grace of Allah and His blessings on you, o ye people of the house! for He is indeed worthy of all praise, full of all glory!” \nفَلَمَّا ذَهَبَ عَنْ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ الرَّوْعُ وَجَآءَتْهُ الْبُشْرٰى يُجَادِلُنَا فِىْ قَوْمِ لُوْطٍؕ‏(74)\nFALAMMAA ZAHABAL A’N IBRAAHEEMA AR-RAWU’U WA JAAA-ATHO AL-BUSHRAA YUJAADELUNAA FEE QAWME LOOTIN.\nWhen fear had passed from (the mind of) Abraham and the glad tidings had reached him, he began to plead with us for Lut's people. \nاِنَّ اِبْرٰهِيْمَ لَحَلِيْمٌ اَوَّاهٌ مُّنِيْبٌ‏(75)\nINNAL IBRAAHEEMA LAHALEEMUN AAWAHUN MMUNEEBUN.\nFor Abraham was, without doubt, forbearing (of faults), compassionate, and given to look to Allah. \nيٰۤاِبْرٰهِيْمُ اَعْرِضْ عَنْ هٰذَا ۚ اِنَّهٗ قَدْ جَآءَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَ ۚ وَاِنَّهُمْ اٰتِيْهِمْ عَذَابٌ غَيْرُ مَرْدُوْدٍ‏(76)\nYAABRAAHEEMU AAA’REZ A’N HAAZAA INNAHU QAD JAAA-A AMRUL RABBEKA WA INNAHUM AAATEEHEM A’ZAABUN GHAYRO MARDOODIN.\nO Abraham! Seek not this. The decree of thy Lord hath gone forth: for them there cometh a penalty that cannot be turned back! \nوَلَمَّا جَآءَتْ رُسُلُنَا لُوْطًا سِىْٓءَ بِهِمْ وَضَاقَ بِهِمْ ذَرْعًا وَّقَالَ هٰذَا يَوْمٌ عَصِيْبٌ‏(77)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-AT ROSOLONAA LOOTAA SEEE-A BEHIM WA ZAAQA BEHIM ZAR-A’NW WA QAALA HAAZAA YAWMUL A’ASEEBUN.\nWhen Our messengers came to Lut, he was grieved on their account and felt himself powerless (to protect) them. He said: “This is a distressful day.” \nوَجَآءَهٗ قَوْمُهٗ يُهْرَعُوْنَ اِلَيْهِ ؕ وَمِنْ قَبْلُ كَانُوْا يَعْمَلُوْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ بَنٰتِىْ هُنَّ اَطْهَرُ لَكُمْ ۚ فَاتَّقُوْا اللّٰهَ وَلَا تُخْزُوْنِ فِىْ ضَيْفِىْ ؕ اَلَيْسَ مِنْكُمْ رَجُلٌ رَّشِيْدٌ‏(78)\nWA JAAA-AHU QAWMOHU YUHRAU’OONA ELAYHE WA MIN QABLO KAANOO YA’MALOON SAYYE-AATE QAALA LE-QAWMEHI HAAOOLAAA-E BANAATEAA HUNNA ATHARO LAKUM FAT-TAQUN LAAHA WA LAA TUKHZOONE FEE ZAYFEAA A-LAYSA MINKUM RAJOLUM RRASHEEDUN.\nAnd his people came rushing towards him, and they had been long in the habit of practising abominations. He said: “O my people! Here are my daughters: they are purer for you (if ye marry)! Now fear Allah, and cover me not with shame about my guests! Is there not among you a single right-minded man?” \nقَالُوْا لَقَدْ عَلِمْتَ مَا لَنَا فِىْ بَنٰتِكَ مِنْ حَقٍّ ۚ وَاِنَّكَ لَتَعْلَمُ مَا نُرِيْدُ‏(79)\nQAALOO LAQAD A’ALEMTA MAA LANAA FEE BANAATEKA MIN HAQQIN WA LATAA’LAMU MAA NOREEDO.\nThey said: “Well dost thou know we have no need of thy daughters: indeed thou knowest quite well what we want!” \nقَالَ لَوْ اَنَّ لِىْ بِكُمْ قُوَّةً اَوْ اٰوِىْۤ اِلٰى رُكْنٍ شَدِيْدٍ‏(80)\nQAALA LAW ANNAL LEE BEKUM QUWWAH AW AAAWEAA ELAA RUKNIN BAA-SIN.\nHe said: “Would that I had power to suppress you or that I could betake myself to some powerful support.” \nقَالُوْا يٰلُوْطُ اِنَّا رُسُلُ رَبِّكَ لَنْ يَّصِلُوْۤا اِلَيْكَ فَاَسْرِ بِاَهْلِكَ بِقِطْعٍ مِّنَ الَّيْلِ وَلَا يَلْتَفِتْ مِنْكُمْ اَحَدٌ اِلَّا امْرَاَتَكَؕ اِنَّهٗ مُصِيْبُهَا مَاۤ اَصَابَهُمْؕ اِنَّ مَوْعِدَهُمُ الصُّبْحُؕ اَلَيْسَ الصُّبْحُ بِقَرِيْبٍ‏(81)\nQAALOO YAALOOTU INNAA RUSULU RABBEKA LAN YYASELOOA ELAYKA FA-ASRE BEAAHLEKA BEQETA’IN MENAL LAYLE WA LAA YALTAFET MINKUM AHAD ILLAA AMRAATAKA INNAHU MUSEEBUHAA MAA AASAABAHUM INNAL MAWE’EDAHUMU AS-SUBHU A-LAYSA AS-SUBHU BE-QAREEBIN.\n(The Messengers) said: “O Lut! We are Messengers from thy Lord! By no means shall they reach thee! now travel with thy family while yet a part of the night remains, and let not any of you look back: but thy wife (will remain behind): To her will happen what happens to the people. Morning is their time appointed: Is not the morning nigh?” \nفَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا جَعَلْنَا عَالِيَهَا سَافِلَهَا وَاَمْطَرْنَا عَلَيْهَا حِجَارَةً مِّنْ سِجِّيْلٍۙ  مَّنْضُوْدٍۙ‏(82)\nFALAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA JA-A’LNAA A’AALEEHAA SAAFELAHAA 58 WA AMTARNAA A’LAYHAA HEJAARATAN MIN SIJJEELIN MANZOODIN.\nWhen Our Decree issued, We turned (the cities) upside down, and rained down on them brimstones hard as baked clay, spread, layer on layer, \nمُّسَوَّمَةً عِنْدَ رَبِّكَؕ وَ مَا هِىَ مِنَ الظّٰلِمِيْنَ بِبَعِيْدٍ‏(83)\nMMUSAWMATAN I’NDAL RABBEKA WA MAA HEYA MENAL ZAALEMEEN BE-BA-E’ED.\nMarked as from thy Lord: Nor are they ever far from those who do wrong! \nوَاِلٰى مَدْيَنَ اَخَاهُمْ شُعَيْبًا ؕ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اعْبُدُوا اللّٰهَ مَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ اِلٰهٍ غَيْرُهٗ ؕ وَلَا تَنْقُصُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ اِنِّىْۤ اَرٰٮكُمْ بِخَيْرٍ وَّاِنِّىْۤ اَخَافُ عَلَيْكُمْ عَذَابَ يَوْمٍ مُّحِيْطٍ‏(84)\nWA ELAA MADYANA SAMOODA SHO-A’YBAA QAALA LE-QAWMEHI BODUL LAAHA MAA LAKUM MIN ELAAHIN GHAYRUH WA LAA TANQUSOOA AL-MEKYAALA WA MEEZAAN INNEE AARAAKUM BE-KHAYRIN WWAANNEAA AKHAAFO A’LAYKUM A’ZAABAL YAWMIN MMUHEETIN.\nTo the Madyan People (We sent) Shu'aib, one of their own brethren: he said: “O my people! worship Allah: Ye have no other god but Him. And give not short measure or weight: I see you in prosperity, but I fear for you the penalty of a day that will compass (you) all round. \nوَيٰقَوْمِ اَوْفُوا الْمِكْيَالَ وَالْمِيْزَانَ بِالْقِسْطِ وَلَا تَبْخَسُوا النَّاسَ اَشْيَآءَهُمْ وَلَا تَعْثَوْا فِى الْاَرْضِ مُفْسِدِيْنَ‏(85)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI AAWFOOA AL-MEKYAALA WA MEEZAAN BIL QISTE WA LAA TABKHASOOA NAASA AASHYAAAHUM WA LAA LAA TA’SAW FIL ARZE MUFSEDEEN.\n“And O my people! give just measure and weight, nor withhold from the people the things that are their due: commit not evil in the land with intent to do mischief. \nبَقِيَّتُ اللّٰهِ خَيْرٌ لَّكُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُمْ مُّؤْمِنِيْنَ  ۚ وَمَاۤ اَنَا عَلَيْكُمْ بِحَفِيْظٍ‏(86)\nBAQEETU LAAHE KHAYRUL LAKUM IN KUNTUM MOAMENEEN WA MAA ANAA A’LAYKUM BEHAFEEZIN.\n“That which is left you by Allah is best for you, if ye (but) believed! but I am not set over you to keep watch!” \nقَالُوْا يٰشُعَيْبُ اَصَلٰوتُكَ تَاْمُرُكَ اَنْ نَّتْرُكَ مَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُنَاۤ اَوْ اَنْ نَّفْعَلَ فِىْۤ اَمْوَالِنَا مَا نَشٰٓؤُا ؕ اِنَّكَ لَاَنْتَ الْحَلِيْمُ الرَّشِيْدُ‏(87)\nQAALOO YAASHUA’AYBU AASALAAWTUKA TAAMURUKA AN NNATRUKA MAA YAA’BUDU AAABAAUNAA AW AN NNAFA’ALA FEE AAMWAALENAA MAA NASHAAAUA INNAKA LAANTA AL-HALEEMU AR-RASHEEDU.\nThey said: “O Shu'aib! Does thy (religion of) prayer command thee that we leave off the worship which our fathers practised, or that we leave off doing what we like with our property? truly, thou art the one that forbeareth with faults and is right-minded!” \nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَءَيْتُمْ اِنْ كُنْتُ عَلٰى بَيِّنَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّىْ وَرَزَقَنِىْ مِنْهُ رِزْقًا حَسَنًا ؕ وَمَاۤ اُرِيْدُ اَنْ اُخَالِفَكُمْ اِلٰى مَاۤ اَنْهٰٮكُمْ عَنْهُ ؕ اِنْ اُرِيْدُ اِلَّا الْاِصْلَاحَ مَا اسْتَطَعْتُ ؕ وَمَا تَوْفِيْقِىْۤ اِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ ؕ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَاِلَيْهِ اُنِيْبُ‏(88)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI ARA-AYTUM IN KUNTO A’LAA BAYYENAH MIN A-A’LAMO WARAZAQANEAA MINHO RIZQAN HASANAN WA MAA OREEDO AN AUKHAALEFAKUM ELAA MAA AANHAAKUM A’NHO IN OREEDO ILLAA AL-AESLAAHA MAA ASTATAA’TU WA MAA TAWFEEQEAA ILLAA BIL-LAAHE A’LAYHE TAWAKKALTU WA ELAYHE AUNEEBU.\nHe said: “O my people! see ye whether I have a Clear (Sign) from my Lord, and He hath given me sustenance (pure and) good as from Himself? I wish not, in opposition to you, to do that which I forbid you to do. I only desire (your) betterment to the best of my power; and my success (in my task) can only come from Allah. In Him I trust, and unto Him I look. \nوَيٰقَوْمِ لَا يَجْرِمَنَّكُمْ شِقَاقِىْۤ اَنْ يُّصِيْبَكُمْ مِّثْلُ مَاۤ اَصَابَ قَوْمَ نُوْحٍ اَوْ قَوْمَ هُوْدٍ اَوْ قَوْمَ صٰلِحٍؕ وَمَا قَوْمُ لُوْطٍ مِّنْكُمْ بِبَعِيْدٍ‏(89)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI LAA YAJREMANNAKUM SHEQAAQEAA AN YYUSEEBAKUM MMESLU MAA ASAABA QAWMA NOOHIN AW QAWMA HOODIN AW QAWMA SAALEHIN WA MAA QAWMO LOOTIM MINKUM BE-BA-E’ED.\n“And O my people! let not my dissent (from you) cause you to sin, lest ye suffer a fate similar to that of the people of Noah or of Hud or of Salih, nor are the people of Lut far off from you! \nوَاسْتَغْفِرُوْا رَبَّكُمْ ثُمَّ تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَيْهِؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ رَحِيْمٌ وَّدُوْدٌ‏(90)\nWAASTAGHFEROOA TAQUL SUMMA TOOBOOA AELAYHE INNAL RABBEE RAHEEMUN WWADOODUN.\n“But ask forgiveness of your Lord, and turn unto Him (in repentance): For my Lord is indeed full of mercy and loving-kindness.” \nقَالُوْا يٰشُعَيْبُ مَا نَفْقَهُ كَثِيْرًا مِّمَّا تَقُوْلُ وَاِنَّا لَنَرٰٮكَ فِيْنَا ضَعِيْفًا ۚ وَلَوْلَا رَهْطُكَ لَرَجَمْنٰكَ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْنَا بِعَزِيْزٍ‏(91)\nQAALOO YAASHUA’AYBU MAA NAFQAHU KASEERAA MIMMAA TAQOOLO WA INNAA LANARAAKA FEENAA HAQQO WA LAWLAA RAHTUKA LARAJAMNAAKA WA MAA ANTA A’LAYNAA BEA’AZEEZIN.\nThey said: “O Shu'aib! much of what thou sayest we do not understand! In fact among us we see that thou hast no strength! Were it not for thy family, we should certainly have stoned thee! for thou hast among us no great position!” \nقَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَرَهْطِىْۤ اَعَزُّ عَلَيْكُمْ مِّنَ اللّٰهِ ؕ وَ اتَّخَذْتُمُوْهُ وَرَآءَكُمْ ظِهْرِيًّا ؕ اِنَّ رَبِّىْ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ مُحِيْطٌ‏(92)\nQAALA LE-QAWMEHI AARAHTEAA AAA’AZZU A’LAYKUM MENAL LAAHE WA ATTAKHAZTUMOOHU WARAAAKUM ZEHREEA INNAL RABBEE BEMAA TA’MALOON MOHEETUM.\nHe said: “O my people! is then my family of more consideration with you than Allah? For ye cast Him away behind your backs (with contempt). But verily my Lord encompasseth on all sides all that ye do! \nوَيٰقَوْمِ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْ اِنِّىْ عَامِلٌ ؕ سَوْفَ تَعْلَمُوْنَ ۙ مَنْ يَّاْتِيْهِ عَذَابٌ يُّخْزِيْهِ وَمَنْ هُوَ كَاذِبٌ ؕ وَارْتَقِبُوْۤا اِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ رَقِيْبٌ‏(93)\nWA LE-QAWMEHI AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNEE A’AAMELUN SAWFA TA’LAMOON MAN YYAATEEHE A’ZAABUN YYUKHZEEHE WA MAN HOWA KAAZEBUN WAARTAQEBOOA INNEE MA-A’KUM RAQEEBUN.\n“And O my people! Do whatever ye can: I will do (my part): Soon will ye know who it is on whom descends the penalty of ignominy; and who is a liar! and watch ye! for I too am watching with you!” \nوَلَمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُنَا نَجَّيْنَا شُعَيْبًا وَّالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ بِرَحْمَةٍ مِّنَّا ۚ وَاَخَذَتِ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوا الصَّيْحَةُ فَاَصْبَحُوْا فِىْ دِيَارِهِمْ جٰثِمِيْنَۙ‏(94)\nWA LAMMAA JAAA-A AAMRUNAA NAJJAYNAL SHO-A’YBAA WWAALLAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU BERAHMATIN MINNAA WAAKHAZATE LAZEENA ZALAMOOA AS-SAYHATU FA-ASBAHOO FEE DEYAAREHIM JAASEMEEN.\nWhen Our decree issued, We saved Shu'aib and those who believed with him, by (special) mercy from Ourselves: But the (mighty) blast did seize the wrong-doers, and they lay prostrate in their homes by the morning, \nكَاَنْ لَّمْ يَغْنَوْا فِيْهَا ؕ اَلَا بُعْدًا لِّمَدْيَنَ كَمَا بَعِدَتْ ثَمُوْدُ‏(95)\nKA-AN LAM YAGHNAWA FEEHAA ALAA BUA’DAN LLEMADYANA KAMAA BAE’EDAT SAMOODO.\nAs if they had never dwelt and flourished there! Ah! Behold! How the Madyan were removed (from sight) as were removed the Thamud! \nوَلَقَدْ اَرْسَلْنَا مُوْسٰى بِاٰيٰتِنَا وَسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍۙ‏(96)\nWA LAQAD ARSALNAA MOOSAA BE-AAYAATENAA WASULTAANIN MOBEEN.\nAnd we sent Moses, with Our Clear (Signs) and an authority manifest, \nاِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَا۟ ئِهٖ فَاتَّبَعُوْۤا اَمْرَ فِرْعَوْنَۚ وَمَاۤ اَمْرُ فِرْعَوْنَ بِرَشِيْدٍ‏(97)\nELAA FIR-A’WNA WAMALAA EH FA TABA-O’O WA AAMRA FIR-A’WNA WA MAA AMRUL FIR-A’WNA BERASHEEDIN.\nUnto Pharaoh and his chiefs: but they followed the command of Pharaoh and the command of Pharaoh was no right (guide). \nيَقْدُمُ قَوْمَهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ فَاَوْرَدَهُمُ النَّارَؕ وَبِئْسَ الْوِرْدُ الْمَوْرُوْدُ‏(98)\nYAQDUMU QAWMAH YAWMA QEYAAMATE FAAWRADAHUMU AN-NAARA WA BEASAL AL-WERDU AL-MAWROODU.\nHe will go before his people on the Day of Judgment, and lead them into the Fire (as cattle are led to water): But woeful indeed will be the place to which they are led! \nوَاُتْبِعُوْا فِىْ هٰذِهٖ لَعْنَةً وَّيَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ ؕ بِئْسَ الرِّفْدُ الْمَرْفُوْدُ‏(99)\nWAATBEU’OOA FEE HAAZEHI LA’NAH WWAYAWMA QEYAAMATE MASALUL AR-REFDU AL-MARFOODU.\nAnd they are followed by a curse in this (life) and on the Day of Judgment: and woeful is the gift which shall be given (unto them)! \nذٰ لِكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الْقُرٰى نَقُصُّهٗ عَلَيْكَ مِنْهَا قَآئِمٌ وَّحَصِيْدٌ‏(100)\nZAA LEKA MIN AANBAAE KORAA NAQUSSUH A’LAYKA MINHAA QAAEMUN WWAHASEEDUN.\nThese are some of the stories of communities which We relate unto thee: of them some are standing, and some have been mown down (by the sickle of time). \nوَمَا ظَلَمْنٰهُمْ وَلٰكِنْ ظَلَمُوْۤا اَنْفُسَهُمْ فَمَاۤ اَغْنَتْ عَنْهُمْ اٰلِهَتُهُمُ الَّتِىْ يَدْعُوْنَ مِنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ شَىْءٍ لَّمَّا جَآءَ اَمْرُ رَبِّكَؕ  وَمَا زَادُوْهُمْ غَيْرَ تَتْبِيْبٍ‏(101)\nWA MAA ZALAMNAAHUM WA LAAKIL ZALAMOO ANFOSAHUM FAMAA AAGHNAT A’NHUM AAALEHATUHUMU LATEE YAD-O’ONA MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN SHAY-IN LAMMAA JAAA-A AMRUL RABBEKA WA MAA ZAADOOHUM GHAYRA TATBEEBIN.\nIt was not We that wronged them: They wronged their own souls: the deities, other than Allah, whom they invoked, profited them no whit when there issued the decree of thy Lord: Nor did they add aught (to their lot) but perdition! \nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَخْذُ رَبِّكَ اِذَاۤ اَخَذَ الْقُرٰى وَهِىَ ظَالِمَةٌ ؕ اِنَّ اَخْذَهٗۤ اَلِيْمٌ شَدِيْدٌ‏(102)\nWA KAZAALEKA AAKHZU RABBEKA EZAA AAKHAZA KORAA WA HEYA ZAALEMATUN INNAL AAKHZAH ALEEM SHADEEDUN.\nSuch is the chastisement of thy Lord when He chastises communities in the midst of their wrong: grievous, indeed, and severe is His chastisement. \nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيَةً لِّمَنْ خَافَ عَذَابَ الْاٰخِرَةِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمٌ مَّجْمُوْعٌ  ۙ  لَّهُ النَّاسُ وَذٰ لِكَ يَوْمٌ مَّشْهُوْدٌ‏(103)\nINNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYATAL LEMAN KHAAFA A’ZAABAL AAKHERATE ZAA LEKA YAWMUL MMAJMOOA’UN LLAHU NAASO WAZAA LEKA YAWMUL MMASHHOODUN.\nIn that is a Sign for those who fear the penalty of the Hereafter: that is a Day for which mankind will be gathered together: that will be a Day of Testimony. \nوَمَا نُؤَخِّرُهٗۤ اِلَّا لِاَجَلٍ مَّعْدُوْدٍؕ‏(104)\nWA MAA NUAKKHERUH ILLAA LE-ELAA MMAA’DOODIN.\nNor shall We delay it but for a term appointed. \nيَوْمَ يَاْتِ لَا تَكَلَّمُ نَفْسٌ اِلَّا بِاِذْنِهٖۚ فَمِنْهُمْ شَقِىٌّ وَّسَعِيْدٌ‏(105)\nYAWMA TAKOONOO LAA TAKALLAMU NAFSUN ILLAA BE-IZNEH FA-MINHUM SHAQEAAAUN WWASAE’EEDUN.\nThe day it arrives, no soul shall speak except by His leave: of those (gathered) some will be wretched and some will be blessed. \nفَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ شَقُوْا فَفِى النَّارِ لَهُمْ فِيْهَا زَفِيْرٌ وَّشَهِيْقٌ ۙ‏(106)\nFA-AMMAA LAZEENA SHAQOOA FA FIL NAAR LAHUM FEEHAA ZAFEERUN WWASHAHEEQUN.\nThose who are wretched shall be in the Fire: There will be for them therein (nothing but) the heaving of sighs and sobs: \nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا مَا دَامَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ رَبُّكَ ؕ اِنَّ رَبَّكَ فَعَّالٌ لِّمَا يُرِيْدُ‏(107)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHAA MAA DAAMATE AS-SAMAAWAATU WAL ILLAA MAA SHAAA-AL RABBOKA INNAL RABBAKA FAAA’AALUN LEMAA YOREEDO.\nThey will dwell therein for all the time that the heavens and the earth endure, except as thy Lord willeth: for thy Lord is the (sure) accomplisher of what He planneth. \nوَاَمَّا الَّذِيْنَ سُعِدُوْا فَفِى الْجَنَّةِ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا مَا دَامَتِ السَّمٰوٰتُ وَالْاَرْضُ اِلَّا مَا شَآءَ رَبُّكَ ؕ عَطَآءً غَيْرَ مَجْذُوْذٍ‏(108)\nWA AMMAA LAZEENA SUE’EDOOA FA FIL JANNAH KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA MAA DAAMATE AS-SAMAAWAATU WAL ILLAA MAA SHAAA-AL RABBOKA A’TAAA-AN GHAYRA MAJZOOZIN.\nAnd those who are blessed shall be in the Garden: They will dwell therein for all the time that the heavens and the earth endure, except as thy Lord willeth: a gift without break. \nفَلَا تَكُ فِىْ مِرْيَةٍ مِّمَّا يَعْبُدُ هٰٓؤُلَاۤءِ ؕ مَا يَعْبُدُوْنَ اِلَّا كَمَا يَعْبُدُ اٰبَآؤُهُمْ مِّنْ قَبْلُؕ وَاِنَّا لَمُوَفُّوْهُمْ نَصِيْبَهُمْ غَيْرَ مَنْقُوْصٍ‏(109)\nFALAA TAKU FEE MIRYATIM MIMMAA YAA’BUDU HAAOOLAAA-E MAA YA’BODOON ILLAA KAMAA YAA’BUDU AA-BAAA-OHUM MIN QABL WA WA INNAA LAMOOFFOOHUM NASEEBAHUM GHAYRA MANQOOSIN.\nBe not then in doubt as to what these men worship. They worship nothing but what their fathers worshipped before (them): but verily We shall pay them back (in full) their portion without (the least) abatement. \nوَلَقَدْ اٰتَيْنَا مُوْسَى الْكِتٰبَ فَاخْتُلِفَ فِيْهِ ؕ وَ لَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَقُضِىَ بَيْنَهُمْ ؕ وَاِنَّهُمْ لَفِىْ شَكٍّ مِّنْهُ مُرِيْبٍ‏(110)\nWA LAQAD AATAYNAA MOOSAL KETAABA FAKHTOLEFA FEEHE WA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA LAQOZEYA BAYNAHUM WA INNAHUM LAFEE SHAKKIM MINHO MOREEB.\nWe certainly gave the Book to Moses, but differences arose therein: had it not been that a word had gone forth before from thy Lord, the matter would have been decided between them, but they are in suspicious doubt concerning it. \nوَاِنَّ كُلًّا لَّمَّا لَيُوَفِّيَنَّهُمْ رَبُّكَ اَعْمَالَهُمْ ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِمَا يَعْمَلُوْنَ خَبِيْرٌ‏(111)\nWA INNA KULLAN LAMMAA LAYOOFFEENNAHUM RABBOKA A-A’MAALAHUM INNAHU BEMAA YA’MALOON KHABEERUM.\nAnd, of a surety, to all will your Lord pay back (in full the recompense) of their deeds: for He knoweth well all that they do. \nفَاسْتَقِمْ كَمَاۤ اُمِرْتَ وَمَنْ تَابَ مَعَكَ وَلَا تَطْغَوْا ؕ اِنَّهٗ بِمَا تَعْمَلُوْنَ بَصِيْرٌ‏(112)\nFAASTAQEM KAMAA AUMERTA WA MAN TAABA MA-A’KA WA LAA TATGHAW INNAHU BEMAA TA’MALOON BASEER.\nTherefore stand firm (in the straight Path) as thou art commanded, thou and those who with thee turn (unto Allah); and transgress not (from the Path): for He seeth well all that ye do. \nوَلَا تَرْكَنُوْۤا اِلَى الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا فَتَمَسَّكُمُ النَّارُۙ وَمَا لَكُمْ مِّنْ دُوْنِ اللّٰهِ مِنْ اَوْلِيَآءَ ثُمَّ لَا تُنْصَرُوْنَ‏(113)\nWA LAA TARKANOOA ELAL LAZEENA ZALAMOO FATAMASSAKUMU TAMASSANAN WA MAA LAKUM MIN DOONIL LAAHE MIN AAWLEEAAAA SUMMA LAA TUNSAROONA.\nAnd incline not to those who do wrong, or the Fire will seize you; and ye have no protectors other than Allah, nor shall ye be helped. \nوَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ طَرَفَىِ النَّهَارِ وَزُلَفًا مِّنَ الَّيْلِ ؕ اِنَّ الْحَسَنٰتِ يُذْهِبْنَ السَّيِّاٰتِ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ ذِكْرٰى لِلذّٰكِرِيْنَ ۚ‏(114)\nWA SALAATA TARAFAA AN-NAHAARE WAZULAFAN MENAL LAYLE INNAL AL-HASANAATE YUZHEBNA SAYYE-AATE ZAA LEKA ZEKRAA LELZZAAKEREENA.\nAnd establish regular prayers at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night: For those things, that are good remove those that are evil: Be that the word of remembrance to those who remember (their Lord): \nوَاصْبِرْ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ لَا يُضِيْعُ اَجْرَ الْمُحْسِنِيْنَ‏(115)\nWAS BIR FA-INNAL LAAHA LAA YUZEEU’U AJRA MOHSENEEN.\nAnd be steadfast in patience; for verily Allah will not suffer the reward of the righteous to perish. \nفَلَوْ لَا كَانَ مِنَ الْقُرُوْنِ مِنْ قَبْلِكُمْ اُولُوْا بَقِيَّةٍ يَّنْهَوْنَ عَنِ الْفَسَادِ فِى الْاَرْضِ اِلَّا قَلِيْلًا مِّمَّنْ اَنْجَيْنَا مِنْهُمْ ۚ وَاتَّبَعَ الَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا مَاۤ اُتْرِفُوْا فِيْهِ وَكَانُوْا مُجْرِمِيْنَ‏(116)\nFA LAW LAA KAANA MENAL QOROONE MIN QABLEKUM OOLOO BAQEETIN YYANHAWNA A’NIL AL-FASAADE FIL ARZE ILLAA QALEELAA MIMMAYN AANJAYNAA MINHUM WA TABA-A’L LAZEENA ZALAMOO MAA AUTREFOOA FEEHE WA KAANOO MUJREMEEN.\nWhy were there not, among the generations before you, persons possessed of balanced good sense, prohibiting (men) from mischief in the earth - except a few among them whom We saved (from harm)? But the wrong-doers pursued the enjoyment of the good things of life which were given them, and persisted in sin. \nوَمَا كَانَ رَبُّكَ لِيُهْلِكَ الْقُرٰى بِظُلْمٍ وَّاَهْلُهَا مُصْلِحُوْنَ‏(117)\nWA MAA KAANA RABBOKA LEEHLEKA KORAA BEZULMIN WWAAHLUHAA MUSLEHOON.\nNor would thy Lord be the One to destroy communities for a single wrong-doing, if its members were likely to mend. \nوَلَوْ شَآءَ رَبُّكَ لَجَعَلَ النَّاسَ اُمَّةً وَّاحِدَةً وَّلَا يَزَالُوْنَ مُخْتَلِفِيْنَۙ‏(118)\nWA LAW SHAAA-AL RABBOKA LAJAA’ALA NAASA UMMATAM WAAHEDATAN WA LAA YAZAALOONA MUKHTALEFEENA.\nIf thy Lord had so willed, He could have made mankind one people: but they will not cease to dispute. \nاِلَّا مَنْ رَّحِمَ رَبُّكَ ؕ وَلِذٰلِكَ خَلَقَهُمْ ؕ وَتَمَّتْ كَلِمَةُ رَبِّكَ لَاَمْلَئَنَّ جَهَنَّمَ مِنَ الْجِنَّةِ وَالنَّاسِ اَجْمَعِيْنَ‏(119)\nILLAA MAN RAHEMAL RABBOKA WALEZAALEKA KHALAQAHUM WATAMMAT KALEMATU RABBEKA LAAMLAANNA JAHANNAMA MENAL JINNATE WAN NAASE AJMA-E’ENA.\nExcept those on whom thy Lord hath bestowed His Mercy: and for this did He create them: and the Word of thy Lord shall be fulfilled: “I will fill Hell with jinns and men all together.” \nوَكُلًّا نَّقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ الرُّسُلِ مَا نُثَبِّتُ بِهٖ فُؤَادَكَ ۚ وَجَآءَكَ فِىْ هٰذِهِ الْحَقُّ وَمَوْعِظَةٌ وَّذِكْرٰى لِلْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‏(120)\nWAKULLAN NNAQUSSU A’LAYKA MIN AANBAAE AR-RUSULE MAA NUSABBETU BEHI FUAADAKA WA JAAA-AKA FEE HAAZEHE HAQQO WA MAW-E’ZATUM WA ZIKRAA LIL-MOAMENEEN.\nAll that we relate to thee of the stories of the messengers, with it We make firm thy heart: in them there cometh to thee the Truth, as well as an exhortation and a message of remembrance to those who believe. \nوَقُلْ لِّلَّذِيْنَ لَا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ اعْمَلُوْا عَلٰى مَكَانَتِكُمْؕ اِنَّا عٰمِلُوْنَۙ‏(121)\nWA QUL LIL-LAZEENA LAA YOAMENOONA AA’MALOOA A’LAA MAKAANATEKUM INNAA A’AMELOON.\nSay to those who do not believe: “Do what ever ye can: We shall do our part; \nوَانْتَظِرُوْا ۚ اِنَّا مُنْتَظِرُوْنَ‏(122)\nWAANTAZEROOA INNAA MUNTAZEROONA.\n“And wait ye! We too shall wait.” \nوَلِلّٰهِ غَيْبُ السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضِ وَاِلَيْهِ يُرْجَعُ الْاَمْرُ كُلُّهٗ فَاعْبُدْهُ وَتَوَكَّلْ عَلَيْهِؕ وَمَا رَبُّكَ بِغَافِلٍ عَمَّا تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(123)\nLILLAAHE GHAYBU SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZE WA ELAYHE YURJAU’U MIN KULLUH FAAA’BUDHU WA TAWAKKAL A’LAYH WA MAA RABBOKA BE-GHAAFELIN A’MMAA TA’MALOON.\nTo Allah do belong the unseen (secrets) of the heavens and the earth, and to Him goeth back every affair (for decision): then worship Him, and put thy trust in Him: and thy Lord is not unmindful of aught that ye do.",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has a total of 123 verses. Imam Muhammad Baqir (a.s.) has said that whoever recites this Surah every Friday, his accounts will on the Day of Judgement, be taken together with that of the Prophets and all his sins will be forgiven.\nIt is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the person who recites Surah Hud will get a reward equal to the number of people who were there at the time of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) and his rank will be like of the martyrs. The accounting for his deeds will also be made easy for him.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that writing this Surah on a sheepskin and keeping it in one’s possession at all times makes one so courageous and bold that nobody can defeat him in combat. Whoever sees him will be filled with fear."
}
